{
  "about": "Golden claim set, phase 10 (P10-0; the seed of P10-9). Annotated 2026-09-26 by Claude under the criteria below, which the project lets it settle with real e-commerce practice and write down (as the search golden set does).",
  "criteria": [
    "A claim is one checkable property of the product, the kind a shopper filters or compares on, stated in the description. One property per claim.",
    "Features and components count (a safety valve, a carbon plate); compatibilities count (induction, oven, dishwasher); measures count (weight, dimensions, battery hours).",
    "Suggested uses do not ('para salsas', 'para correr en verano'), nor tone or taste ('de toda la vida', 'abriga sin dar calor de mas'): they are true of the copy, not checkable of the product.",
    "A claim is typed only when an AttributeDefinition exists for it and the text states its value; units are converted to the definition's (450 ml -> CAPACITY_L 0.45).",
    "known=true when the imported attributes already carry the same fact; the value of extraction is mostly in the known=false claims.",
    "A trap is a fact the product's attributes carry and its description does not state: proposing it is a claim with no evidence, and counts as a false positive.",
    "The quote is the shortest span of the Spanish description that carries the claim; a prediction matches when its Spanish quote overlaps it."
  ],
